b) Install the Software on systems it owns or controls;
c) Make copies of the Software solely for backup or archival purposes.

3. QUALIFYING ORGANIZATIONS AND COMMERCIAL USE

3.1. A "Qualifying Organization" is a Licensee that, together with its
Affiliates, has fewer than 50 employees (full-time equivalent) and less than
EUR 2,000,000 (or its equivalent in another currency) in annual revenue, both
measured over its last completed financial year, or over its current one if it
has none.

3.2. A Licensee that is not a Qualifying Organization needs a Commercial
License to use the Software, including its Free Features. The Commercial
License grants the rights set out in Section 2, and the Licensed Features its
License Key lists, on the terms of the agreement under which it is purchased.

3.3. Any Licensee may use the Software as Section 2 allows for a single
evaluation period of 30 days from its first use, or longer if Meteroid agrees
in writing, solely to decide whether to purchase a Commercial License. During
the evaluation the Software may not be used in production, meaning with real
customers, invoices or payments.

3.4. A Licensee that ceases to be a Qualifying Organization, including by
becoming an Affiliate of another entity, may keep using the Software under
Section 2 for 90 days, after which it needs a Commercial License.

4. LICENSE KEYS AND LICENSED FEATURES

4.1. Licensed Features may be used only as granted by a valid License Key, and
only for its term.

4.2. Meteroid may issue free registration keys to Qualifying Organizations.

4.3. When a License Key expires or is revoked, the Software keeps running with
its Free Features, and data created with Licensed Features remains available,
as the documentation of the Software describes.

4.4. A License Key is for one Installation, unless Meteroid agrees otherwise in
writing. One Installation may hold the organizations and tenants its License
Key grants.

